WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.440
A wide, empty moor.

2
00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:05.250
The wind runs through the long grass.

3
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:10.260
A lonely dreamer walks away across
it, looking up at the dark sky.

4
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:14.320
Then, from nowhere,
come words: "Come back,

5
00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.040
and dwell with me."

6
00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.990
There's nobody else on the moor.

7
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.940
So whose voice is it?

8
00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.000
In this mission, you'll
meet a poem with no title,

9
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:26.700
printed in 1850, after
Emily Brontë's death.

10
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.850
You'll hunt through the voice's own
words for clues to who is speaking.

11
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.770
And you'll follow it from
gentle questions to a command.

12
00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:37.730
Your mission: work out whose voice it is.
